				\begin{document}$$\sqrt{{\rm{SWAP}}}$$\end{document}SWAP gate between atomic qubits in natural silicon26. Exchange gates on electron spins have also been implemented with gate-defined quantum dots in isotopically pure silicon with fidelities greater than 99% (refs. 27–30). Successful implementation of exchange gates in atom qubits have already been achieved in purified silicon-28 (ref. 31), yet the limited two-qubit gate fidelity challenges the applicability of quantum-error-correction protocols32,33.

